# Generated assets — COMMITTED ON PURPOSE, do not re-ignore.
#
# These are build products, and ignoring them is the usual instinct. It was
# also the reason the deployed site rendered in Times: scripts/fonts.mjs
# fetches Sora from fonts.googleapis.com and Switzer from api.fontshare.com,
# so with public/fonts ignored, every deploy had to reach two third-party
# hosts mid-build to produce a font the CSS already references by path. When
# that failed the woff2 files 404'd and every face fell back to serif.
#
# public/fonts   100K, 6 files  — the only ones that need the network
# public/audio   564K, 3 files  — synthesised, deterministic
# public/img     4.2M, 135 files — sharp-derived from src/assets/*.jpg
#
# The images and audio do regenerate offline, but committing them makes the
# deploy deterministic and drops ~135 sharp encodes off the build: no native
# binary to install, nothing to re-derive, nothing that can differ between a
# laptop and a build container.
#
# Refresh them with `bun run images` / `bun run fonts` / `bun run audio` and
# commit the result.

# Local secrets. .env.example is the committed template.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
